{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KfbzfqvEKEDZqczJDZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<final_document>\nGood evening, commissioners. I'm Captain Ray Dunn. I've run the charter boat Sea Lark out of our harbor for 22 years, about 160 trips a season.\n\nI don't dispute your staff's numbers. The stock is at 78 percent of target, and it needs help. I'm here to ask you to give it that help with a 3-fish limit or a shorter season instead of cutting to 2 fish.\n\nHere's what I know from my own books. The last time the limit was cut, in 2016, my bookings fell from 170 trips to 138 the next season. That's 32 trips, close to $29,000 at today's rates. It took two years to climb back to 155, and I never got back to 170.\n\nThis time looks worse. Our charter association surveyed 70 past customers. Forty-one said they would book fewer trips at 2 fish. Only 12 said they'd book the same.\n\nThere are 11 charter boats in our harbor. I can only speak for my own books. But two other captains have told me that if bookings fall the way they did in 2016, they'll sell. Each boat that goes takes crew jobs and customers that the docks, tackle shops and restaurants count on.\n\nCharter boats land about 9 percent of the state's summer flounder. Private boats land about 80. For a private angler, 2 fish means a shorter day. For us, it decides whether customers book at all.\n\nWe want to help you get the data right. I'll give your staff my trip logs from 2016 on, and our association will test a catch-reporting app with your staff next season.\n\nPlease choose a 3-fish limit or a shorter season. Either one lets the stock recover and keeps our boats running. Thank you.\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes before you use it:\n\n- **Length:** It's about 290 words, which runs close to two minutes at a normal pace. Time yourself reading it out loud. If you need to cut, drop the private-boat comparison first.\n- **The harbor point:** I kept it to what you can stand behind: what's in your books, what two captains told you, and what a lost boat means for the docks. Nothing in it claims boats will close.\n- **The association commitment:** You weren't sure you can speak for the association. Before the hearing, confirm they'll back testing the reporting app. If they won't, change that line to \"I'll ask our association to test…\"\n- **\"At today's rates\":** This is there because your 2016 price may not have been $900. If you know the 2016 price, you can use the actual dollar figure.\n- **What I left out:** I didn't mention that 70% of your trips are already booked. A commissioner could take it as a sign that demand is fine. If someone asks, you can answer honestly: those customers booked expecting a 4-fish limit, and you don't yet know how many will keep their trips."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1327,"cache_read_input_tokens":10205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1327},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d794da83-6bcf-420e-ab03-952b1affa427","uuid":"25581f42-b397-467c-8c0a-f8d956982ef9","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:32:59.264Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Kfbm2gEwYAYuHKjQhJ"}
